<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">China</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chinese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">China is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, home to one of the world's oldest continuous civilisations, unified under successive dynasties including the Han, Tang, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, Yuan, Ming and Qing. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> and other goods drew trade across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, linking it to empires from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>. Steppe powers such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Göktürks</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> alternately raided, extracted tribute from and conquered it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/china.jpg" alt="China" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zeng Liansong · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
